# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ── Design tooling, not project code ────────────────────────
# The vendored Impeccable skill: ~2.1MB across 51 files, and half the tracked
# size of this repo. It is a tool, reinstallable with `npx impeccable install`,
# so it does not belong in a repo the band or another developer will hold.
#
# What it PRODUCES does stay tracked, because that is the actual value:
# PRODUCT.md, DESIGN.md and .impeccable/design.json are the design contract.
.claude/skills/
.claude/agents/

# Detector hook cache. Ephemeral, rewritten on every UI edit.
.impeccable/hook.cache.json

# ── Not code, and not for a public repo ─────────────────────
# 205MB of Instagram exports. Evidence the design was measured from, not
# shippable source — and the photography belongs to the photographers
# (@danielblakevisuals and others), so it must not be redistributed here.
/heavyskint-insta-images/

# Commercial engagement plan: running costs, margins, VAT position, payment
# rates and account-ownership strategy. Fine on your machine, wrong in a repo
# the band or another developer may end up holding.
/heavyskint-website-plan.md

# Impeccable live-mode session state (ephemeral). Note that
# .impeccable/config.json, .impeccable/design.json and .impeccable/live/config.json
# ARE project config and stay tracked — they're the design contract.
/.impeccable/live/sessions/
/.impeccable/live/annotations/
/.impeccable/live/roots.json
/.impeccable/live/server.json
/.impeccable/live/inject-journal.json

# Scratch space
/.scratch/
